Sure it can.  It's unlikely to be particularly easy, of course, but
whatever.

Personally, I'd start by finishing the job on that priest.  This is
debatable, but I wouldn't want to accidentally run into an ambush.  The
negative is that you'll lose all your protection and telepathy to boot;
the positive is that you'll (still) be able to use the altar to clean
up after your mess, and you've got at least two other temples in the
game at which to donate all of the money that will be on your
newly-deceased priest's corpse.  Just don't sacrifice the priest's
corpse on the altar; and you might consider taking the priest out from
outside the temple, if you can arrange it.  Better yet, have pets do it
for you, if you can swing that.

After the priest was dead, I'd go use the money on the Minetown priest
to regain the protection, and possibly consider a sacfest to regain the
favor of my god.  But probably not; prayer (past the early game) is
rarely necessary.

After that, I'd look at doing the quest (-30 AC is overkill for the Arc
quest, which is mostly a bunch of snakes and mummies) and then head
down past Medusa.  What scrolls in particular were you hoping to have
by this point?

